Artifact: learning/status.json 2026-09-20 23:53 UTC — maturation {matured 0, pending 0, unavailable 200}
every tick, errors 0; outcomes.jsonl 131,980 rows over 14,731 opportunities, 4-12 new rows an hour since
2026-09-20 04:00; 6,941 judge looks in 48 h with no outcome row.

Cause: an episode with a SHORT-stage row whose data then left the live window was settled at its deadline by
pushing a COPY of the existing row (same attachedTs, same supersedes). The store's duplicate check dropped it
silently; the episode never left the pending set; the oldest 200 such episodes consumed the whole sweep budget
on every tick, so the newest judge looks were never labelled and FIX-86's counterfactual produced nothing.

Fix: the settlement is a new attachment — this sweep's clock, superseding the row it settles. The tick report
names settledAtDeadline / skippedRecent / written so a stalled sweep is visible in status.

Test: test/publish-fix-92-settle-supersedes.test.js (fails on the previous code). Neighbours green:
learning-maturation, learning-service, publish-fix-86-live-counterfactual, research-maturation, learning-fences.

